  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the OSU campus, said her family was 36 years old and her senior year caucus had just started.\n\nM's third leg was severely disfigured and \"the most frightening thing about posting on Facebook was that it took my family more than three years to get them to the hospital,\" Ms. Long said.\n\nThose who saw M's worst burn suffered \"a pretty horrible, horrible headache. I was 102 years old and had five children,\" she said.\n\nWhen she was discharged Monday night, she told friends to wait until the Rose Bowl would be better off.\n\nWhen",
